WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:08.400
To map a venue, an organizer walks the public areas with a phone. Whereabout measures the walls and doors as they go.

00:09.500 --> 00:15.900
Saying a landmark's name as they pass it adds it to the map. Signs and booth names are read on their own.

00:18.600 --> 00:21.720
In a few minutes of walking, the whole floor is mapped.

00:22.500 --> 00:25.910
Publish it, and the map is live for everyone who joins.

00:27.000 --> 00:31.550
Attendees join with the event's six-letter code, and the map is on their phone.

00:33.500 --> 00:37.960
Then they ask the way in their own words: where they are, and where they want to go.

00:40.000 --> 00:42.970
The answer comes in words, one stretch at a time.

00:43.600 --> 00:48.060
Whereabout Spaces. Map the floor once, and everyone finds their way.
